We should store the temporary lock data in MySQL together with the existing PPI Tracker backend data. MongoDB is not required for this feature.

The lock data will be stored separately from the actual tracker values. It will include the project, entity, optional field name, current editor, lock token, and expiry time.

For the full Edit Entity dialog, the system will create a lock for the selected entity or entities. For Edit in Cell, the system will create a lock only for the specific cell.

The lock will be released when the user saves, cancels, or closes the editor. If the application closes unexpectedly, the lock will expire automatically after a short period.

I have prepared the MySQL table design separately.

